# Core conventions

Project: `stock_pick_strat` — Python quant long/short stock-picking pipeline.
Stack: Python, OmegaConf (`DictConfig`), pandas, SQLAlchemy + PostgreSQL (Docker), OpenAI, pytest.
Configs: `configs/*.yml`, loaded via OmegaConf — never hardcode config values inline.
OS: Windows PowerShell; run Python via the project's Poetry venv.

## Architecture
- A chain of `Step` classes (`src.utils.step`); each `src/` subfolder owns a `step_*.py` orchestrator
  (a super-step may compose sub-steps in the same folder). `run()` is the only public entry point and
  calls helpers from the SAME folder.
- **All tabular data lives in PostgreSQL**, via `context.store` (`DataStore`) — never parquet.
  `context.paths` is only for non-tabular artifacts (models, plots, JSON/zip caches, filing text).

## Naming — constants first
Before naming any column, key, URL, or literal: check `src/constants/constants.py`. Reuse if present;
add it there before using if not. Never hardcode global literals inline.

## Data / DB
- Read/write tables via `context.store.load / save / replace / existing_dates`; new columns auto-add
  via `ensure_columns`. Fetchers save to the DB (return the frame), resume from the DB max date per
  entity, save per entity, and are point-in-time (filing-date lag → leak-free).
- Cache large downloads (companyfacts JSON, 13F zips) to disk; re-download only when missing.

## Anti-patterns
- No cross-folder imports between `src/` subfolders — shared logic goes in `src/utils/`.
- No `print()` for logging — use `self._log` (steps) / `context.log` (helpers).
- Never write tabular data to parquet/CSV — use `context.store`.
- Sanity-check real-data edge cases before declaring done; tests must print a sanity conclusion.

## Docs
Keep the `.cursor/rules`, `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `README.md` in sync with the code; propose &
confirm a new convention before adding it. Keep this file short — it loads on every call.

## Commands
- `pytest tests/path/to/test_file.py::test_fn -v -s`   (`-s` shows the sanity-check print)
